Chick Season Begins FEBRUARY 2026
Pullets available late APRIL 2026
PULLET sales beginning MAY. Sales are on a first-come-first-serve basis. Pullets will be available until FALL.
Get baby chicks along with all the supplies you need to start your flock with us!
Our chicks will arrive beginning February 20th. Sales begin on Chick Days for each batch until we sell out.

See Availability
What You'll Need

Our first chicks of the season arrive February 20, 2026!

Availability, hatch dates, and breed information will be posted in January 2026.

Get your baby chicks — plus all the feed, brooders, heat lamps, and supplies you need to start your flock — right here in one stop.

Pullets will be available April/May 2026.
Our first Pullet Day will be announced in early April 2026.

All chick and pullet sales are first-come, first-served and available while supplies last.

Questions? We’re happy to help — please don’t hesitate to contact us.

*Chick sales may be limited on chick day depending on availability and customer demand. If demand is high (defined as 20 or more customers in line), we will temporarily limit purchases to ensure as many families as possible have an opportunity to buy chicks. If demand is not high, customers may purchase as many chicks as they wish.

*All chicks are sold on a first-come, first-served basis. We do not offer holds or reservations. However you may place special orders ahead of time.

*Baby chicks are FINAL SALE. Please remember they are only a few days old and are extremely delicate creatures. Unfortunately you can do EVERYTHING correctly and still lose them for unknown reasons.

*All chicks have been vaccinated for Marek

*Standard breeds are sexed however gender selection is about 90% accurate on average. Bantams and specialty breeds are NOT SEXED. If you get a STANDARD BREED rooster you may bring it back WITH PROOF OF PURCHASE. We are happy to help you rehome it. Bantams and specialty breed roosters WILL NOT BE taken back.

